  "title": "Robust Representation Learning",
  "abstract": "Abstract Representation learning models, especially pre-trained models, help NLP systems achieve superior performances on multiple standard benchmarks. However, real-world environments are complicated and volatile, which makes it necessary for representation learning models to be robust. This chapter identifies different robustness needs and characterizes important robustness problems in NLP representation learning, including backdoor robustness, adversarial robustness, out-of-distribution robustness, and interpretability. We also discuss current solutions and future directions for each problem.",
